</section>

<section>
  <h2>FAQ</h2>

  <h3>What if Google rewrites my meta tags?</h3>
  <p>Google rewrites meta descriptions about 70% of the time, pulling text from your page that better matches the search query. This is normal. Write a good default description, but focus more on having great on-page content.</p>

  <h3>Should I include emojis in meta tags?</h3>
  <p>Emojis can increase clicks but look unprofessional for some industries. Use them for B2C products (✨ Free PDF Tools ✨) but skip them for B2B or professional services.</p>

  <h3>Do meta keywords still matter?</h3>
  <p>No. Google hasn't used the meta keywords tag since 2009. Don't waste time on it.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Conclusion</h2>
  <p>Great meta tags won't make up for bad content, but they're the difference between getting clicks and being ignored.</p>
  <p>Spend 5 minutes crafting perfect meta titles and descriptions for every important page. Your traffic will thank you.</p>
</section>

</BlogPost>